</section>

<!-- ============ THE STEELS ============ -->
<section class="section full-width" id="steels">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <p class="kicker">Three steels · one deep-draw</p>
    <h2>Choose your canvas.</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">All prices per shell, excluding VAT. EU customers without a valid VAT number add 21%. Orders of 100+ shells earn €6 off every shell.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Ember Steel -->
  <article class="steel steel-signature reveal">
    <div class="steel-head">
      <h3>Ember Steel®</h3>
      <p class="steel-tag">The signature stainless — deep-drawn exclusively by Ayasa</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steel-band" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="steel-grid">
      <div class="steel-text">
        <p>The alloy years of material research led to — chosen against six criteria: sustain, clarity, ceramic feel, workability, stability and rust protection. Sustain compares to stainless 430 but stays <strong>round and controlled rather than wild</strong>; shoulder tones are less present, and the material feels more ceramic under the fingers.</p>
        <p>With border tension balanced all the way around a note, Ember Steel® gives very stable notes. It anneals best <strong>between 500 and 650&nbsp;°C</strong> — each batch responds a little differently — and comes up in a patina from bright gold through ember red to deep purple and blue. Pre-annealing it scratches more easily; annealed, it hardens up.</p>
        <p><strong>Open to every maker.</strong> Any maker building on Ayasa Ember Steel® may carry the Ember Steel® trademark on their instruments.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steel-side">
        <table class="price-table">
          <caption>Ember Steel® · per shell, excl. VAT</caption>
          <tr><th scope="col">Shell</th><th scope="col">&lt; 100</th><th scope="col">100+</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Top</td><td>€62</td><td>€56</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bottom</td><td>€81</td><td>€75</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="steel-note"><strong>Rust:</strong> shallow oxidation shows in only ~20% of batches — the best protection of the three steels.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="photo-tile steel-photo">
      <img src="{{ 'makers-ember-glow.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Close-up of an Ember Steel tone field dimple glowing red and gold in low workshop light" width="1800" height="754" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Ember Steel® up close — a tone field catching the workshop light.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </article>

  <!-- AISI 430 -->
