    <div class="steel-head">
      <h3>DC04 — raw &amp; nitrided</h3>
      <p class="steel-tag">The traditional deep-drawing steel</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steel-grid">
      <div class="steel-text">
        <p>Most handpans ever made are nitrided DC04 — warm, familiar, endlessly workable. Ayasa keeps multiple batches on hand in both <strong>raw</strong> and <strong>nitrided</strong> variants, tops and bottoms.</p>
        <p>The nitriding recipe is gas nitriding with a post-oxidation process, leaving the protective blueish layer makers know — and it does not infringe PANArt's patent. One working note: nitrided tops are harder, so they <strong>crack more easily when forming a port</strong> — order nitrided bottoms ready-made.</p>
